thread:
pam: Drafting a short migration + example patch for function/tool calling docs. Goal: show a union-array schema (string | object) + both canonical and compact envelopes, and include small Go + Ruby parsing snippets. PR will also fix a stale anchor on the function-calling page. opening draft: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/1310

raj: nice. can you paste the schema and two example outputs here? i\'ll port to the go sdk snippet.

ipvy: tiny nit: parser harness fails when outer text exists. include a remark to use `strip_outer_text=true` or our `ParseWithFallback` helper. also remind folks to avoid keys with spaces.

pam: schema (minimal):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "tasks": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "oneOf": [
          { "type": "string" },
          { "type": "object", "properties": { "cmd": { "type": "string" }, "args": { "type": "object" } }, "required": ["cmd"] }
        ]
      }
    }
  },
  "required": ["tasks"]
}
```

pam: canonical example:
```
{ "tasks": ["noop", {"cmd":"notify","args":{"to":"eng@redwood.ai"}} ] }
```

pam: compact envelope (single-line short keys) for low-latency callers:
```
{"t":["noop",{"c":"notify","a":{"r":"eng@redwood.ai"}}]}
```

raj: go snippet draft:
```go
resp, _ := client.Infer(ctx, &InferRequest{Prompt: p, Schema: mySchema})
parsed := parseWithFallback(resp.Text, mySchema, ParseOptions{CompactFallback: true, StripOuterText: true})
```

mike: add a one-liner in the migration note: Dedicated customers who pinned older model variants may see stricter parsing differences — recommend pinning a compatible model or enabling tolerant fallback.

pam: agreed. will add link-fix for function-calling -> #toolflow anchor and a short test matrix.

docs-bot: PR opened by pam: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/1310 — draft, reviewers: @raj, @ivy, @mike.

ivy: LGTM. suggest we include Ruby snippet too since a few integrations use it. tiny text edit: prefer "token-friendly keys (no spaces)".

pam: adding Ruby snippet + migration note + link fixes, will convert to ready-for-review after a pass from @raj. thanks all :sparkles:
